cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "M.I.R.A.G.E.: Multimodal Intelligent Rendering & Automated Generation Engine"
message: "If you use M.I.R.A.G.E. or its synthetic perception datasets in your research or engineering systems, please cite this software using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Madupu"
    given-names: "Madhav"
    email: "madhav.madupu@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Applied AI Engineer - Autonomous Systems & AI Infrastructure"
repository-code: "https://github.com/madhavmadupu/mirage"
url: "https://github.com/madhavmadupu/mirage"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic headless synthetic perception dataset generation engine built on
  Blender 4.2 LTS (bpy) and NVIDIA OptiX raytracing for single-GPU workstations
  (NVIDIA RTX 4060 8GB). Implements stratified Latin Hypercube Sampling (LHS)
  for domain randomization, rigid-body physics pose settling, single-pass
  multi-modal ground-truth extraction (RGB, Float32 metric depth, surface
  normals, 16-bit instance segmentation masks, 2D/3D bounding boxes, and 6-DoF
  poses), cryptographic SHA-256 dataset provenance verification, and direct
  export to Ultralytics YOLO11 (R.A.P.T.O.R.), COCO JSON, and WebDataset/LeRobot
  (P.R.I.M.E.).
keywords:
  - synthetic-data
  - computer-vision
  - robotics-perception
  - domain-randomization
  - blender-bpy
  - optix-raytracing
  - 6dof-pose-estimation
  - instance-segmentation
  - yolo11
  - physical-ai
license: Apache-2.0
